title: 1922 Presidential Election 
subtitle: The first presidential election of our young Republic.
view-if: year = 1922 and month >= 2
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
tags: event
face-image: img/Jozef-Pilsudski-Polish-soldiers.webp
on-arrival: {!
for (var party of Q.parties) {
    Q[party + '_pres_votes'] = Math.round(((Q[party + '_sj'] + Q[party + '_sn']) / 2) * 10) / 10;
}

Q.narutowicz_votes = 0;
Q.daszynski_votes = 0;
Q.wojciechowski_votes = 0;
Q.courtenay_votes = 0;
Q.zamoyski_votes = 0;

Q.narutowicz_round = 1;
Q.daszynski_round = 1;
Q.wojciechowski_round = 1;;
Q.courtenay_round = 1;
Q.zamoyski_round = 1;

Q.round = 1;

Q.endorsement_daszynski = 0;
Q.psl_l_choice = 'Narutowicz';
Q.psl_w_choice = 'Narutowicz';
Q.psl_p_choice = 'Wojciechowski';
Q.npr_choice = 'Wojciechowski';
Q.pps_choice = '0';
Q.kpp_choice = '0';
Q.bmn_choice = 'Courtenay';
Q.other_choice = 'Courtenay';
Q.chzjn_choice = 'Zamoyski';

!}

=  1922 Presidential Election

Its time to view the candidates. Now, Piłsudski is expected to run after calls for him to contend from moderates, <span style="color: #c00000;">socialists</span>, and even some right-wing followers- wait, what? Piłsudski isnt running? 

It seems Marshal Piłsudski has decided not to run in these presidential elections, instead, most believe he will attempt to rally the **<span style="color: #CCC;">Pol</span><span style="color: #DC143C;">ish</span>** parties  towards a unity candidate he supports.

After his decision to not put forward a candidacy, many parties have been left scrambling to put forward a candidate that is **not** Piłsudski, due to this decision coming close to the presidential elections.  Now, lets see..

- @who

@who
title: Who will be the successor of Piłsudski?
subtitle: Good question.

Without a unifying figure such as Piłsudski around, many fear the ChZJN might win the presidency, however, Piłsudski must have a plan, right? He wouldnt have dropped out without having a plan. Yes..

Now, from all these possible candidates, Piłsudski's first choice is..

- @witos

@witos
title: Witos Wincenty
face-image: img/portraits/WitosWincenty.jpeg

<span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">Witos Wincenty<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/portraits/WitosWincenty.jpeg">Leader of the PSL-P </br></br> Former Prime-Minister</span></span>, a moderate and leader of the PSL-P, has been suggested as a unity candidate agaisnt the ChZJN by <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">Piłsudski<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/portraits/PilsudskiJozef.jpg">Józef Piłsudski </br></br> Marshal Of Poland</span></span>, however he has declined, and <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">Piłsudski<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/portraits/PilsudskiJozef.jpg">Józef Piłsudski </br></br> Marshal Of Poland</span></span> starts searching for someone else. Now, who is second on his list..

- @narutowicz

@narutowicz
title: Gabriel Narutowicz.
face-image: img/portraits/Narutowicz_Pilsudski.jpg

<span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">Gabriel Narutowitcz<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/portraits/Narutowicz.jpeg">Minister of Foreign Affairs </br></br> Former Minister of Public Works </span></span>, a independent,  has been suggested by <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">Piłsudski<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/portraits/PilsudskiJozef.jpg">Józef Piłsudski </br></br> Marshal Of Poland</span></span> as a unity candidate agaisnt the ChZJN, after <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">Wincenty<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/portraits/WitosWincenty.jpeg">Member of the PSL-P</span></span> refused. However, he still has not officially agreed to this.

 However, <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">Narutowitcz<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/portraits/Narutowicz.jpeg">Minister of Foreign Affairs </br></br> Former Minister of Public Works </span></span>  has still not agreed, and <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">Piłsudski<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/portraits/PilsudskiJozef.jpg">Józef Piłsudski </br></br> Marshal Of Poland</span></span> will have to convince him.. now, lets see..

- @narutoyay
  
@narutoyay
title: Narutowicz accepts!
face-image: img/NarutowiczGabriel.jpg
on-arrival: narutowicz_votes = (psl_l_pres_votes + psl_w_pres_votes)

With <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">Narutowitcz<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/portraits/Narutowicz.jpeg">Minister of Foreign Affairs </br></br> Former Minister of Public Works </span></span> nominated to replace <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">Piłsudski<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/portraits/PilsudskiJozef.jpg">Józef Piłsudski </br></br> Marshal Of Poland</span></span> can he expect the moderates throw their support for him, especially due to some moderates looking at him as a puppet of <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">Piłsudski<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/portraits/PilsudskiJozef.jpg">Józef Piłsudski </br></br> Marshal Of Poland</span></span>?

For better or worse, <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">Narutowitcz<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/portraits/Narutowicz.jpeg">Minister of Foreign Affairs </br></br> Former Minister of Public Works </span></span> did not secure the support of the moderates, However his candidacy is still supported by the PSL-L and PSL-W.

- @candidate

@candidate
title: What other candidates are going on the <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">campaign trail<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/campaign_trail.webp">good game</span></span>?

- @zamoyski
- @courtenay
- @wojciechowski
- @communist

@zamoyski
title: Maurycy Zamoyski.
subtitle: A non-partisan candidate fielded by the ChZJN. Largest estate and the biggest land owner. Serving as the **<span style="color: #CCC;">Pol</span><span style="color: #DC143C;">ish</span>** envoy to **<span style="color: #000091;">Pa</span><span style="color: #CCC;">r</span><span style="color: #E1000F;">is</span>**.
on-arrival: candidate += 1; zamoyski_votes = (zln_pres_votes + pschd_pres_votes + otherright_pres_votes)
go-to: candidate
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/portraits/ZamoyskiMaurycy.jpg

<span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">Maurycy Zamoyski<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/portraits/ZamoyskiMaurycy.jpg">Richest Polish Noble</span></span>, one of **<span style="color: #CCC;">Pol</span><span style="color: #DC143C;">and</span>**'s wealthiest landowners and its envoy to **<span style="color: #000091;">Pa</span><span style="color: #CCC;">r</span><span style="color: #E1000F;">is</span>** he is the candidate of the ChZJN. His nationalist and aristocratic background, combined with his experience in foreign affairs as part of the **<span style="color: #CCC;">Pol</span><span style="color: #DC143C;">ish</span>** delegation to the **Paris Conference**, which concluded with the signing of the Treaty of Versailles, makes him the preferred candidate of the ChZJN.

His candidacy is supported by the ChZJN.

@courtenay
title: Jan Baudouin de Courtenay.
subtitle: **<span style="color: #CCC;">Pol</span><span style="color: #DC143C;">ish</span>** and <span style="color: #CCC;">**Ru**</span><span style="color: #0036A7;">**ssi**</span><span style="color: #D62718;">**an**</span> Linguist and a staunch supporter for Minority rights.
on-arrival: candidate += 1; courtenay_votes = (bmn_pres_votes + other_pres_votes)
go-to: candidate
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/portraits/CourtenayJan.jpg

<span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">Jan Baudouin de Courtenay<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/portraits/CourtenayJan.jpg">Linguist</span></span> is a relative obscure candidate, known for his theory of Phoneme. His candidacy was proposed by the BMN due to  him being a strong supporter of the national revival of various national minority and ethnic groups, taking a relatively pro-minority stance.

Even though <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">Jan Baudouin<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/portraits/CourtenayJan.jpg">Linguist</span></span> isn't expected to win, His candidacy is supported by the BMN and the other minority parties as a show of solidarity against right-wing dominance.

@wojciechowski
title: Stanisław Wojciechowski.
subtitle: Previously a member of our party, the PPS.
on-arrival: candidate += 1; wojciechowski_votes = (npr_pres_votes + psl_p_pres_votes)
go-to: candidate
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/portraits/WojciechowskiStanisław.jpg

<span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">Witos Wincenty<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/portraits/WitosWincenty.jpeg">Leader of the PSL-P </br></br> Previous Prime-Minister</span></span> has been a bit unpopular with the more moderate wings of the PSL-P, primarily due to his right-wing tendencies and many saying he was not paying attention to the rural villages.  Hence, <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">Stanisław Wojciechowski<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/portraits/WojciechowskiStanisław.jpg">Member of the PSL-P</span></span> has been  fielded as a compromise candidate representing the Centrist and Moderates of the PSL-P. Surprisingly, he was previously a member of our party.

His candidacy is supported by the PSL-P and NPR.

@communist
title: How about the Communists?
view-if: candidate >= 3

The KPP has decided to boycott the presidential election.

- @pps

@pps
title: So, what is our decision? Should we run our own candidate?

- @daszynskielection: Run <span style="color: #C62828;">Ignacy Daszyński</span> of the PPS.
- @narutowiczelection: Support Narutowicz as a unity candidate.
- @wojciechowskielection: Support <span style="color: #3A6538;">Wojciechowski</span> of the PSL-P.

@daszynskielection
subtitle: This is the default choice 
on-arrival: pps_choice = 'Daszynski'; daszynski_votes = pps_pres_votes

We have chosen to field <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">Ignacy Dasyznski<span class="wide_tooltip-tip"><img src="img/portraits/DaszyńskiIgnacy.jpg"> Leader of the PPS </span></span>.

- @scouting: Scout out potential endorsement.

@scouting

We can't win this election alone, we need support from other parties.

- @npr_scout: Convice the NPR to support <span style="color: #C62828;">Ignacy Daszyński</span>
- @psl_l_scout: Convice the PSL-L to support <span style="color: #C62828;">Ignacy Daszyński</span>
- @psl_w_scout: Convice the PSL-W to support <span style="color: #C62828;">Ignacy Daszyński</span>
- @psl_p_scout: Convice the PSL-P to support <span style="color: #C62828;">Ignacy Daszyński</span>
- @bmn_scout: Convince the BMN to support <span style="color: #C62828;">Ignacy Daszyński</span>
- @viewscout: View party endorsements.
- @scoutdone: We have concluded negotiating with other parties.

